  "conclusion": "On Logic in ja-JP, the four track-header checkboxes were found by the descriptions isMuted by 'ミュート', isSoloed by 'ソロ', isArmed by '録音を可能にする', isInputMonitoring by '入力モニタリング', each the value of Apple's row this record cites. In the readings where logic://tracks served rows a header read wrote (A_all_on, B_solo_released, C_all_off), 23 of the 24 cells whose checkbox read 0 or 1 were published as that value. In A_all_on, track 3's isMuted was left out of the row while the walk after the read read 0, as did the walk before it; the tally counts it as disagreeing. It is the Mute of the track the solo silenced, the checkbox the limits name as reading -1 in some walks and 0 in others; which value the product's own read met is not recorded. Against the record this supersedes, read with the build of 693c02fd whose MCU parser wrote the Mute LED into isMuted: reads that served the rows MCU feedback creates went from 6 of 8 to 0 of 3, and reads whose muted rows were exactly the first MCU bank's strips other than the soloed track (the LED's pattern) went from 2 to 0. Verdict partial by the rule in the tally.",
  "limits": [
    "One host and one disposable project (the 19-track locale-campaign fixture); track 2 carries the toggles and track 3 is the one read off. Other builds, other track types and a hidden or collapsed header are not measured.",
    "Logic draws a soloed track's own Mute checkbox as 0, so no single reading shows all four on: reading A has Solo, Record Enable and Input Monitoring on, reading B has Mute, Record Enable and Input Monitoring on.",
    "While a track is soloed, the Mute checkbox of every track the solo silences read -1 in some walks and 0 in others; the product publishes a -1 as unread and a 0 as false, and which one its read meets depends on when it lands. A cell whose walk after the read met -1 is counted apart, not compared; one whose walk met 0 while the product left the field out is counted as disagreeing, and nothing records which value the product's own read met.",
    "A logic://tracks read is compared with the header walk taken right after it, not at the same instant; the walk before the read is recorded, and ax_same_before_and_after_the_read says whether the header moved in between.",
    "Input Monitoring was set and cleared by the harness (AXFocused, then AXPress on the checkbox), not by the product, which has no Input Monitoring write.",
    "No read in this run, in any locale, served the rows MCU feedback creates, so this run does not show what such a row publishes while a solo lights the Mute LED of the tracks it silences; Issue1040MCUMuteLEDTests feeds that LED and checks logic://tracks and the audit.",
